Steam Enhanced, client/game-page/page.js: no layout reads in a scroll frame.

Why. placeScrolled() runs once per frame while a scroller scrolls. Measured on a game page
(2 s of scrolling, Steam's ScrollToTopButton present): placeScrolled 177-229 ms of its own time
(scrollHeight / scrollTop / offsetWidth reads that force the layout count there), plus
getBoundingClientRect 39-51 ms and querySelectorAll 45-54 ms; 26-68 frames/s.
Two causes:
  - placeTop() set --se-scroll on the button and then read four boxes: the write made every read
    after it recompute the styles and the layout, every frame;
  - a scroll re-measured the button's place, though a scroll does not move it (the scroller's
    box moves on a resize, which topSizer and onResizeTop already handle);
  - and a scroller no button served was searched again on every frame (querySelectorAll plus
    two boxes per button in servesScroller()).

What. placeTop(btn, scrollOnly): on a scroll of a placed button only the progress is read and
set; every read comes before every write. A scroller no button serves is remembered (WeakMap)
with the number of buttons there were, and is not searched again until that number changes.

